#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203856 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204102 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6600adba-92a6-523c-b214-9e506bc37cc9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients of Linear Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "8ad540bc-bc15-5b57-aa7a-1ea46693a4e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-17348" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f: \\mathbb{R}^4 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by ![](images/47/471a898dd8e3dca3d9e0b077a135ac794ef58293dafa33703d23490dd92d12b6.svg) with respect to $\\mathbf{x}$ at ![](images/55/552dda7785a5e118e9ff3afa9bf7e7201e7d3be7454e7e380c42946d60506f31.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Writing ![](images/e0/e0ec0bd3b3ed1126735e229d153c206900bdff443354b04700379343ab15e876.svg), we have\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x})= \\mathbf{b}^T\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nThe gradient of a function $f(x) = \\mathbf{b}^T\\mathbf{x}$ with respect to $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ is\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n![](images/4f/4f11665969b8a11e45fe97ef4f3add0115b365642e92e21172e2245e61147f31.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203864 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204103 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7de7a9a-4848-5590-b066-f746262181e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients Including Squared Norms"}] :question/id #uuid "d50d20a4-2c3e-5469-8ced-2fde5d6690e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-17754" :question/problem "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{w}) = -7\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x} + 3\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|^2 - 2\n$$\n\nthat maps two vectors to a scalar, find $\\nabla_{\\mathbf w} f .$" :question/worked-solution "Using the results \n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}(\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}, \\qquad \\nabla_{\\mathbf w} (\\mathbf{w}^T\\mathbf{w}) = 2\\mathbf{w},\n$$\n\n \nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(-7{w}^{T}x+3‖w{‖}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)+3\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}^{2})-{∇}_{w}(2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)+3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)-{∇}_{w}(2) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot x+3\\cdot 2w-0 \\\\  & =-7x+6w.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203874 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204104 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86b3efb7-511d-5da7-92ca-5add976b1ca1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients of Functions Containing L1 Norms"}] :question/id #uuid "5222f4d3-4fec-545c-b9f3-4d8a8e84d2c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-18710" :question/problem "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{w}) = -3\\left(\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|_1\\right)^3  - 5\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w\n$$\n\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find $\\nabla_{\\mathbf w}f.$ You may assume that $\\mathbf w$ has no zero components." :question/worked-solution "Using the results\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf w} (\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|_1) = \\text{sign}(\\mathbf{w}), \\qquad \\nabla_{\\mathbf w}\\left(\\mathbf x^T\\mathbf w\\right) = \\mathbf x,\n$$\n\n we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(-3{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}-5{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}(-3{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})-{∇}_{w}(5{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})-5\\cdot {∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})-5\\cdot x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-5\\cdot x \\\\  & =-9(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532624 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204102 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6600adba-92a6-523c-b214-9e506bc37cc9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients of Linear Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58920a3a-358f-5d1e-8e4c-a50997ac4a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532127} {:answer/id #uuid "65b1e62d-8397-5718-92b4-3cc4c0404c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532158} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8027b8-6be4-57a7-a65f-2e31748d8ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532172} {:answer/id #uuid "e45f0f82-ca1e-522b-beb2-25f53e90f4da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532421} {:answer/id #uuid "e89b9918-d9b6-5ede-a900-7264152a3a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "‖x‖" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e45f0f82-ca1e-522b-beb2-25f53e90f4da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532421} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5c58c75-9e77-56fd-b251-39036e32bd87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0446f1ce-7aff-5c2b-b94d-259fd188ab51" :question/math-academy-id "q-264920" :question/problem "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(x,w)={w}^{T}x+4\n$$\n\nthat maps two vectors to a scalar, find ${∇}_{w}f.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the result \n\n$$\n{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)=x,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x+4) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)+{∇}_{w}(4) \\\\  & =x+0 \\\\  & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204103 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7de7a9a-4848-5590-b066-f746262181e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients Including Squared Norms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8333ad5c-643c-532a-a7ae-6d46ae048983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203359} {:answer/id #uuid "bf