$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot x\n$$\n\n with respect to $x$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Writing $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)={b}^{T}x.\n$$\n\nThe gradient of a function $f(x)={b}^{T}x$ with respect to $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204104 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86b3efb7-511d-5da7-92ca-5add976b1ca1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients of Functions Containing L1 Norms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080f7321-9bc8-5ade-99cd-67f832dfd7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)+w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531952} {:answer/id #uuid "55c18f25-6f5e-5d0b-8df7-f3fa1e5f1ef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{sign}(w)+2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532120} {:answer/id #uuid "89f6ccba-5549-5421-855d-3dfda87c6847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{sign}(w)+w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532246} {:answer/id #uuid "ac994e05-1946-5fd8-9faa-6ab8c770a092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{sign}(w)+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532320} {:answer/id #uuid "e4040a0e-21e7-5bae-a634-08b7855b6c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4040a0e-21e7-5bae-a634-08b7855b6c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532420} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e221444-1ca4-5f83-b8a3-c4d4f75a3ed7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "662b9c53-b55a-5b63-9768-b5b6d98e927b" :question/math-academy-id "q-275961" :question/problem "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(x,w)=4{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}+{x}^{T}w\n$$\n\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find ${∇}_{w}f.$ You may assume that $w$ has no zero components." :question/worked-solution "Using the results\n\n$$\n{∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})=\\text{sign}(w),\\,{∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w)=x,\n$$\n\n we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(4{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}+{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}(4{(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})+{∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})+{∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})+x \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)+x \\\\  & =12(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204103 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7de7a9a-4848-5590-b066-f746262181e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradients Including Squared Norms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "083c30b1-6494-5f7f-a514-ca4c654a14b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531953} {:answer/id #uuid "47f56299-6e42-5254-9516-56c603e5c09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2‖w‖" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532080} {:answer/id #uuid "935bd9b2-fb76-558f-97bd-419defc9c8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "‖w‖+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592